 "method": "W7-STAGE7: first stage 7 art from the shared static export (predicted-static; import only after a live capture confirms the key).\nusage: python build_s7.py planet|explosion|hulls [freeze]     -> staging/<name>/  (freeze: frozen/<name>/, immutable)\n\nSource: remaster-audit/fullgame-prep/static-extraction/stages/stage7 (textures/<TEX>.words.bin exact-static, cluts.json; the\nstage CLUT block 4/18 at (0,480,256,20)+(0,504,256,8)); crc32 of the words == TEX and of every CLUT == PAL re-checked.\n\nIndex master (CLUT-free, one per page, 8 px/texel = the 2048 export grid): per-index soft weights.  For every native index i the\none-hot mask is upsampled texel-centred (bilinear), gaussian-smoothed (sigma, texels) and raised to a power, then normalised; the\nmaster keeps the top-K labels and weights per pixel (u8).  Any CLUT renders it: RGB = weighted mix of the CLUT entries of the\nvisible labels; alpha either 'soft' (visibility = weight of visible labels >= 0.5, class of the strongest visible label) or\n'native' (the native class map, nearest).  Then the native class is forced at every native texel centre floor((i+0.5)*scale)\n(one pixel each) and validated (0 mismatches).\nRecipes (all CPU, deterministic, no AI, nothing added):\n  planet    sigma 0.90, power 1.0, top-4, alpha native: the limb pages are ordered-dithered tone images with stippled\n            (alternating transparent column) fades; a linear soft mix of the visible labels turns the dither into continuous\n            tone (motion-safe); the stipple columns are the native class map (they cannot become partial alpha: classes are\n            categorical).\n  explosion sigma 0.45, power 1.5, top-4, alpha native (w2-effects FX contract: alpha = native class map, RGB free); per frame\n            cell the light energy of every preview render is checked against native (0.95-1.05).\n  hulls     sigma 0.30, power 4.0, top-3, alpha soft (w4-world catsoft: plateaus keep exact native colours, stair steps\n            become smooth contours).\nKey exports only for listed predicted keys with a real (non-zero) CLUT; renders with other stage CLUTs are review previews.",
